SUMMARY:Deadline 23:59 EST: A.I.R. Gallery: Fellowship Program 2027-2028 (N
 YC)
DESCRIPTION:Closes 10 Nov 2026 at 23:59 EST.\n\nThe A.I.R. Fellowship Progr
 am for Emerging and Underrepresented Women and Non-Binary Artists\, establ
 ished in 1993 by artist Stephanie Bernheim\, annually awards six emerging 
 artists based in New York City their first solo exhibition in NYC with the
  support of the A.I.R. community\; more than 130 artists have come through
  the program. WHAT YOU GET: a USD 3\,000 stipend\, a solo exhibition at A.
 I.R.\n\nOrganisation: A.I.R. Gallery\nLocation: New York City. Applicants 
 must be residents of the five boroughs for the full fellowship duration.\n
 Award: USD 3\,000 stipend per fellow\, plus a solo exhibition at A.I.R. Ga
 llery\, 4 to 5 professional development workshops\, an assigned artist-men
 tor\, a studio visit with a review panelist and ongoing staff support. Six
  fellows selected. No application fee stated.\nDuration: 12-month fellowsh
 ip\, September 2027 to August 2028\; solo exhibition in spring/summer 2028
 \n\nMore: https://www.airgallery.org/fellowship-program-2027-2028?utm_sour
 ce=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.airgallery.org/fellowship-program-2027-2028?utm_source=arti
 ficialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:New York City. Applicants must be residents of the five boroughs f
 or the full fellowship duration.
END:VEVENT
