SUMMARY:Deadline: The Center Fellowship for Justice-Impacted Artists (Cente
 r for Art & Advocacy\, US)
DESCRIPTION:The Center Fellowship (formerly Right of Return)\, run by The C
 enter for Art & Advocacy\, supports formerly incarcerated artists with an 
 annual award of USD 10\,000 in unrestricted funds and USD 10\,000 in proje
 ct development funds.\n\nOrganisation: The Center for Art & Advocacy\nLoca
 tion: USA. Open to US-based\, directly justice-impacted artists regardless
  of citizenship status\, felony convictions\, or formal arts training.\nAw
 ard: USD 10\,000 in unrestricted funds plus USD 10\,000 in project develop
 ment funds per fellow\, awarded annually.\nDuration: One-year fellowship c
 ohort\, including an annual retreat with previous fellows\, advocates\, in
 dustry leaders\, and funders.\n\nMore: https://centerforartandadvocacy.org
 /programs?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral#fellow
 ship
URL:https://centerforartandadvocacy.org/programs?utm_source=artificialnouve
 augrantdesk&utm_medium=referral#fellowship
LOCATION:USA. Open to US-based\, directly justice-impacted artists regardle
 ss of citizenship status\, felony convictions\, or formal arts training.
END:VEVENT
